   "fadeIn": 0.25,
   "fadeOut": 0.3
  },
  {
   "text": "Unity on Mono",
   "start": 15.308,
   "duration": 8.788,
   "x": 560,
   "y": -230,
   "fontSize": 40,
   "bgColor": "#0b1a3a",
   "bgOpacity": 0.85,
   "bgPadding": 18,
   "outline": 0,
   "color": "#eafffb",
   "fadeIn": 0.25,
   "fadeOut": 0.3
  },
  {
   "text": "third-party assemblies: 0",
   "start": 15.758,
   "duration": 8.338,
   "x": -560,
   "y": 60,
   "fontSize": 40,
   "bgColor": "#0b1a3a",
   "bgOpacity": 0.85,
   "bgPadding": 18,
   "outline": 0,
   "color": "#eafffb",
   "fadeIn": 0.25,
   "fadeOut": 0.3
  },
  {
   "text": "no DoNotShip folder",
   "start": 16.208,
   "duration": 7.888,
   "x": 560,
   "y": 60,
   "fontSize": 40,
   "bgColor": "#0b1a3a",
   "bgOpacity": 0.85,
   "bgPadding": 18,
   "outline": 0,
   "color": "#eafffb",
   "fadeIn": 0.25,
   "fadeOut": 0.3
  },
  {
   "text": "This horror demo promises no jumpscares. Its build quietly\nmakes the same kind of promise about everything else.",
   "start": 0.0,
   "duration": 6.472
  },
  {
   "text": "There is exactly one non-engine\nassembly in it. One.",
   "start": 6.722,
   "duration": 3.886
  },
  {
   "text": "Let's do the game first.",
   "start": 14.458,
   "duration": 1.508
  },
  {
   "text": "The No Jumpscare Show. In its world the paranormal is ordinary,\nand jumpscares are a lazy cliche everybody is tired of.",
   "start": 16.216,
   "duration": 7.83
  },
  {
   "text": "So a girl called Illy signs up for a haunted house that advertises\nthe opposite. Real psychological horror, no cheap shots.",
   "start": 24.296,
   "duration": 8.065
  },
  {
   "text": "Survive the night without getting scared\nand you win ten thousand dollars.",
   "start": 32.611,
   "duration": 4.121
  },
  {
   "text": "It's black and white. All of it. Not drained of colour afterwards,\nbuilt that way, with checkerboard floors and paper faces.",
   "start": 41.982,
   "duration": 7.308
  },
  {
   "text": "And the monsters have names, and they talk to you. Thingy. Skelly\nBilly. Manicus, who says hello and thanks you for coming to the show.",
   "start": 49.54,
   "duration": 8.483
  },
  {
   "text": "That's the joke and the threat in one move. Nothing\nleaps out. Things walk up and start a conversation.",
   "start": 58.273,
   "duration": 6.341
  },
  {
   "text": "It went up yesterday. English only, four\nreviews, and a full game with no date on it.",
   "start": 64.864,
   "duration": 5.322
  },
  {
   "text": "Which leaves the build.",
   "start": 70.436,
   "duration": 1.456
  },
  {
   "text": "Three hundred and thirty-nine megabytes.\nTwo hundred and sixty-two files.",
   "start": 72.142,
   "duration": 4.486
  },
  {
   "text": "Unity, on the Mono backend. Mono matters here, because it\nmeans the assembly list is readable instead of compiled away.",
   "start": 76.878,
   "duration": 7.543
  },
  {
   "text": "That list is where every one of these episodes has found its\nstory. Who they bought from. What they forgot to take out.",
   "start": 84.671,
   "duration": 7.099
  },
  {
   "text": "So here is this\none, in full.",
   "start": 92.02,
   "duration": 2.161
  },
  {
   "text": "Assembly-CSharp. Their own code,\ncompiled. And then nothing.",
   "start": 94.431,
   "duration": 4.8
  },
  {
   "text": "No DOTween. No Odin. No Steamworks wrapper, no asset-store\nshaders, no text animator, no save system, no pathfinding library.",
   "start": 99.481,
   "duration": 9.319
  },
  {
   "text": "A haunted-house demo that went up the same\nday carries more than forty of those.",
   "start": 109.05,
   "duration": 4.591
  },
  {
   "text": "There's no StreamingAssets folder\neither. No Plugins folder.",
   "start": 113.891,
   "duration": 3.65
  },
  {
   "text": "And no folder called BackUpThisFolder_ButDontShipItWithYourGame. Unity writes\nthat name for you, and three demos I've opened this month shipped it anyway.",
   "start": 117.791,
   "duration": 8.901
  },
  {
   "text": "The hundred and eight DLLs\nin here are all Unity's own.",
   "start": 126.942,
   "duration": 3.52
  },
  {
   "text": "So if three hundred megabytes didn't\ngo into packages, where did it go?",
   "start": 130.712,
   "duration": 4.121
  },
  {
   "text": "Into the rooms. level10 on its own is seventy-two\nmegabytes. One scene, twenty-one percent of the game.",
   "start": 135.083,
   "duration": 6.628
  },
  {
   "text": "Ninety-eight megabytes of resource files and sixty-two of resS beside it. Audio and\ntextures, sitting exactly where Unity leaves them when nobody has built a pipeline.",
   "start": 141.961,
   "duration": 11.357
  },
  {
   "text": "It is the plainest build I\nhave opened on this channel.",
   "start": 153.568,
   "duration": 2.945
  },
  {
   "text": "Reception is four reviews and one day.\nThere's nothing to read there yet.",
   "start": 156.763,
   "duration": 4.121
  },
  {
   "text": "So here's the honest read. This is what it looks like when\na small team writes the thing and doesn't go shopping.",
   "start": 161.134,
   "duration": 6.21
  },
  {
   "text": "That is not automatically better, and I want to be clear about it. Bought packages\nare how small teams ship at all. I've said exactly that about six demos in a row.",
   "start": 167.594,
   "duration": 9.371
  },
  {
   "text": "But after fifteen builds where the story was what somebody\nleft in, a list with nothing on it is worth stopping on.",
   "start": 177.215,
   "duration": 6.21
  },
  {
   "text": "Here's the whole\nteardown on one card.",
   "start": 183.675,
   "duration": 2.266
  },
  {
   "text": "Unity on Mono, three hundred and thirty-nine megabytes, two hundred and\nsixty-two files, and one assembly that isn't the engine's — which is theirs.",
   "start": 186.191,
   "duration": 9.032
  },
  {
   "text": "Worth a dip. It's free, it's genuinely strange, and a monster that\nintroduces itself politely turns out to be worse than one that jumps.",
   "start": 195.473,
   "duration": 7.961
  },
  {
   "text": "If you ship in Unity, open your own Managed folder and count what's in it.\nThere's no prize for a short list. But there is a lot of information in yours.",
   "start": 203.684,
   "duration": 8.979
  },
  {
   "text": "That's my read from the outside. If you worked on this and I\ngot something wrong, say so and I'll pin the correction. Next\ntime, another demo, another file list. This is Demo Dip.",
   "start": 212.913,
   "duration": 9.371,
   "fontSize": 42
  }
 ],
